  blockers:
    - id: PRODUCER-POLICY-RESOLUTION-BINDING
      statement: >-
        The frozen producer receipt requested coordinator-orchestration-code
        but launched gpt-5.6-sol while the frozen binding resolved that policy
        to gpt-5.6-terra. The receipt verifies a short probe, not the later
        authoring tokens; no permitted fallback or inference amendment repairs
        this mismatch.
    - id: HA2-EXPECTATION-NOT-TAIL
      statement: >-
        The HA-2 values are expectations only. They give no tuplewise,
        simultaneous-tail, or worst-case guarantee, so a positive-probability
        thirty-third distinct value remains compatible with the stated mean.
    - id: SYSTEM-PEAK-LIVE-CONCURRENCY
      statement: >-
        System peak must be computed as
        max_t(shared(t)+sum_j concurrent_nonshared_shard_j(t)-dedup(t)), not as
        a maximum over isolated per-shard peaks. The required KAT binds eight
        simultaneous shards, one staggered shard, and shared allocation counted
        exactly once.
    - id: RT-OBJ3
      status: open_non_blocking_deferred
      statement: crossover-N estimate remains open and deferred.
    - id: RT-OBJ4
      status: open_non_blocking_deferred
      statement: k-list/generalized-birthday baseline remains open and deferred.
    - id: CAPACITY-RESIDUALS
